{"assets":["/statement-assets/65726d1ba98ed002e969732210caf04645a8c069af08422dd561fa96c9b03dd1.png","/statement-assets/5094a1510d943e21cdc42242b2a1a86ab9715619659bed51a2a13d534a433304.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1228","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Filling the Grid"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Suppose there is a $$$h \\times w$$$ grid consisting of empty or full cells. Let's make some definitions:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$r_{i}$$$ is the number of consecutive full cells connected to the left side in the $$$i$$$-th row ($$$1 \\le i \\le h$$$). In particular, $$$r_i=0$$$ if the leftmost cell of the $$$i$$$-th row is empty. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$c_{j}$$$ is the number of consecutive full cells connected to the top end in the $$$j$$$-th column ($$$1 \\le j \\le w$$$). In particular, $$$c_j=0$$$ if the topmost cell of the $$$j$$$-th column is empty. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In other words, the $$$i$$$-th row starts exactly with $$$r_i$$$ full cells. Similarly, the $$$j$$$-th column starts exactly with $$$c_j$$$ full cells."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/65726d1ba98ed002e969732210caf04645a8c069af08422dd561fa96c9b03dd1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"These are the $$$r$$$ and $$$c$$$ values of some $$$3 \\times 4$$$ grid. Black cells are full and white cells are empty."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have values of $$$r$$$ and $$$c$$$. Initially, all cells are empty. Find the number of ways to fill grid cells to satisfy values of $$$r$$$ and $$$c$$$. Since the answer can be very large, find the answer modulo $$$1000000007\\,(10^{9} + 7)$$$. In other words, find the remainder after division of the answer by $$$1000000007\\,(10^{9} + 7)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$h$$$ and $$$w$$$ ($$$1 \\le h, w \\le 10^{3}$$$) — the height and width of the grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$h$$$ integers $$$r_{1}, r_{2}, \\ldots, r_{h}$$$ ($$$0 \\le r_{i} \\le w$$$) — the values of $$$r$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains $$$w$$$ integers $$$c_{1}, c_{2}, \\ldots, c_{w}$$$ ($$$0 \\le c_{j} \\le h$$$) — the values of $$$c$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the answer modulo $$$1000000007\\,(10^{9} + 7)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 4\n0 3 1\n0 2 3 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 1\n0\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n19 16\n16 16 16 16 15 15 0 5 0 4 9 9 1 4 4 0 8 16 12\n6 12 19 15 8 6 19 19 14 6 9 16 10 11 15 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n797922655\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, this is the other possible case."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/5094a1510d943e21cdc42242b2a1a86ab9715619659bed51a2a13d534a433304.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, it's impossible to make a grid to satisfy such $$$r$$$, $$$c$$$ values."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, make sure to print answer modulo $$$(10^9 + 7)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1228B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1228/problem/B"}